m one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[10]},{"id":"moab_2103","name":"Moab","also":"Moabitess, Moabitish, Moabites","summary":"Used to denote the people of Moab (Num. 22:3-14; Judg. 3:30; 2 Sam. 8:2; Jer. 48:11, 13).","verses":149,"father":"Lot","mother":"Daughter of Lot - Older","v":[11,13,15,20,26,28,29]},{"id":"sihon_2739","name":"Sihon","also":"","summary":"Striking down. The whole country on the east of Jordan, from the Arnon to the Jabbok, was possessed by the Amorites, whose king, Sihon, refused to permit the Israelites to pass through his territory, and put his army in array against them.","verses":34,"father":"","mother":"","v":[21,23,26,27,28,29,34]},{"id":"chemosh_931","name":"Chemosh","also":"","summary":"The destroyer, subduer, or fish-god, the god of the Moabites (Num. 21:29; Jer. 48:7, 13, 46). The worship of this god, “the abomination of Moab,” was introduced at Jerusalem by Solomon (1 Kings 11:7), but was abolished by Josiah (2 Kings 23:13).","verses":8,"father":"","mother":"","v":[29]},{"id":"og_2238","name":"Og","also":"","summary":"Gigantic, the king of Bashan, who was defeated by Moses in a pitched battle at Edrei, and was slain along with his sons (Deut. 1:4), and whose kingdom was given to the tribes of Reuben and Gad and half the tribe of Manasseh (Num. 21:32-35; Deut. 3:1-13).","verses":22,"father":"","mother":"","v":[33]}],"places":[{"id":"arad_81","name":"Arad","kind":"City","lat":31.28098,"lon":35.12637,"summary":"Now Tell Arad, a Canaanite city, about 20 miles south of Hebron. The king of Arad “fought against Israel and took of them prisoners” when they were retreating from the confines of Edom (Num. 21:1; 33:40; Judg. 1:16).","verses":4,"v":[1]},{"id":"atharim_117","name":"Atharim","kind":"","lat":30.88092,"lon":34.63062,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[1]},{"id":"negeb_885","name":"Negeb","kind":"Region","lat":30.25,"lon":34.75,"summary":"Heb. Negeb, that arid district to the south of Palestine through which lay the caravan route from Central Palestine to Egypt (Gen. 12:9; 13:1, 3; 46:1-6).","verses":36,"v":[1]},{"id":"hormah_580","name":"Hormah","kind":"","lat":30.88092,"lon":34.63062,"summary":"Banning; i.e., placing under a “ban,” or devoting to utter destruction. After the manifestation of God’s anger against the Israelites, on account of their rebellion and their murmurings when the spies returned to the camp at Kadesh, in the wilderness of Paran, with an evil report of the land, they quickly repented of their conduct, and presumed to go up “to the head of the mountain,” seeking to enter the Promised Land, but without the presence of the Lord, without the ark of…","verses":9,"v":[3]},{"id":"edom_357","name":"Edom","kind":"Region","lat":31.25,"lon":34.75,"summary":"Idumea (Isa. 34:5, 6; Ezek. 35:15). “The field of Edom” (Gen. 32:3), “the land of Edom” (Gen. 36:16), was mountainous (Obad. 1:8, 9, 19, 21).","verses":79,"v":[4]},{"id":"mount_hor_842","name":"mount Hor","kind":"Mountain","lat":30.3274,"lon":35.4464,"summary":"One of the mountains of the chain of Seir or Edom, on the confines of Idumea (Num. 20:22-29; 33:37). It was one of the stations of the Israelites in the wilderness (33:37), which they reached in the circuitous route they were obliged to take because the Edomites refused them a passage through their territory.","verses":10,"v":[4]},{"id":"red_sea_986","name":"Red sea","kind":"Water","lat":19.0,"lon":39.5,"summary":"The sea so called extends along the west coast of Arabia for about 1,400 miles, and separates Asia from Africa. It is connected with the Indian Ocean, of which it is an arm, by the Strait of Bab-el-Mandeb.","verses":26,"v":[4]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[5]},{"id":"oboth_906","name":"Oboth","kind":"","lat":31.49685,"lon":35.78284,"summary":"Bottles, an encampment of the Israelites during the wanderings in the wilderness (Num. 33:43), the first after the setting up of the brazen serpent.","verses":4,"v":[10,11]},{"id":"iye-abarim_606","name":"Iye-abarim","kind":"","lat":31.49685,"lon":35.78284,"summary":"","verses":2,"v":[11]},{"id":"moab_815","name":"Moab","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.49916,"lon":35.78051,"summary":"The land of Moab (Jer. 48:24), called also the “country of Moab” (Ruth 1:2, 6; 2:6), on the east of Jordan and the Dead Sea, and south of the Arnon (Num. 21:13, 26).","verses":148,"v":[11,13,15,20,26,28,29]},{"id":"valley_of_zered_1224","name":"valley of Zered","kind":"Valley","lat":30.88413,"lon":35.89763,"summary":"Zared, luxuriance; willow bush, a brook or valley communicating with the Dead Sea near its southern extremity (Num. 21:12; Deut. 2:14). It is called the “brook of the willows” (Isa. 15:7) and the “river of the wilderness” (Amos 6:14).","verses":1,"v":[12]},{"id":"arnon_92","name":"Arnon","kind":"Water (River)","lat":31.25,"lon":35.75,"summary":"Swift, the southern boundary of the territory of Israel beyond Jordan, separating it from the land of Moab (Deut. 3:8, 16). This river (referred to twenty-four times in the Bible) rises in the mountains of Gilead, and after a circuitous course of about 80 miles through a deep ravine it falls into the Dead Sea nearly opposite Engedi.","verses":12,"v":[13,14,24,26,28]},{"id":"suphah_1116","name":"Suphah","kind":"","lat":27.08847,"lon":34.77173,"summary":"(Num. 21:14, marg.; also R.V.), a place at the south-eastern corner of the Dead Sea, the Ghor es-Safieh.","verses":1,"v":[14]},{"id":"waheb_1228","name":"Waheb","kind":"","lat":27.08847,"lon":34.77173,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[14]},{"id":"ar_77","name":"Ar","kind":"","lat":31.44981,"lon":35.59396,"summary":"","verses":6,"v":[15,28]},{"id":"beer_164","name":"Beer","kind":"Fort","lat":30.99806,"lon":35.49855,"summary":"A place where a well was dug by the direction of Moses, at the forty-fourth station of the Hebrews in their wanderings (Num. 21:16-18) in the wilderness of Moab.","verses":1,"v":[16]},{"id":"mattanah_772","name":"Mattanah","kind":"","lat":31.71815,"lon":35.58483,"summary":"A gift, a station of the Israelites (Num. 21:18, 19) between the desert and the borders of Moab, in the Wady Waleh.","verses":2,"v":[18,19]},{"id":"bamoth_157","name":"Bamoth","kind":"","lat":31.76503,"lon":35.71857,"summary":"Heights, the forty-seventh station of the Israelites (Num. 21:19, 20) in the territory of the Moabites.","verses":2,"v":[19,20]},{"id":"nahaliel_870","name":"Nahaliel","kind":"Valley","lat":31.71815,"lon":35.58483,"summary":"Possession, or valley of God, one of the encampments of the Israelites in the wilderness (Num. 21:19), on the confines of Moab.","verses":1,"v":[19]},{"id":"pisgah_950","name":"Pisgah","kind":"","lat":31.76503,"lon":35.71857,"summary":"A part, a mountain summit in the land of Moab, in the territory of Reuben, where Balak offered up sacrifices (Num. 21:20; 23:14), and from which Moses viewed the promised land (Deut. 3:27).","verses":5,"v":[20]},{"id":"highway_690","name":"Highway","kind":"","lat":31.18133,"lon":35.70215,"summary":"","verses":2,"v":[22]},{"id":"jahaz_617","name":"Jahaz","kind":"City","lat":31.501,"lon":35.92063,"summary":"Trodden down (called also Jahaza, Josh. 13:18; Jahazah, 21:36; Jahzah, 1 Chr. 6:78), a town where Sihon was defeated, in the borders of Moab and in the land of the Ammonites beyond Jordan, and north of the river Arnon (Num. 21:23; Deut. 2:32).","verses":5,"v":[23]},{"id":"jabbok_609","name":"Jabbok","kind":"Water (River)","lat":32.19324,"lon":35.6763,"summary":"A pouring out, or a wrestling, one of the streams on the east of Jordan, into which it falls about midway between the Sea of Galilee and the Dead Sea, or about 45 miles below the Sea of Galilee.","verses":7,"v":[24]},{"id":"heshbon_565","name":"Heshbon","kind":"City","lat":31.79819,"lon":35.80986,"summary":"Intelligence, a city ruled over by Sihon, king of the Amorites (Josh. 3:10; 13:17). It was taken by Moses (Num. 21:23-26), and became afterwards a Levitical city (Josh. 21:39) in the tribe of Reuben (Num. 32:37).","verses":37,"v":[25,26,27,28,30,34]},{"id":"dibon_331","name":"Dibon","kind":"City","lat":31.49916,"lon":35.78051,"summary":"A city in Moab (Num. 21:30); called also Dibon-gad (33:45), because it was built by Gad and Dimon (Isa. 15:9).","verses":9,"v":[30]},{"id":"medeba_775","name":"Medeba","kind":"City","lat":31.72046,"lon":35.79197,"summary":"Waters of quiet, an ancient Moabite town (Num. 21:30). It was assigned to the tribe of Reuben (Josh. 13:16). Here was fought the great battle in which Joab defeated the Ammonites and their allies (1 Chr. 19:7-15; comp. 2 Sam. 10:6-14).","verses":5,"v":[30]},{"id":"nophah_905","name":"Nophah","kind":"City","lat":32.75692,"lon":36.6164,"summary":"Blast, a city of Moab which was occupied by the Amorites (Num. 21:30).","verses":1,"v":[30]},{"id":"jazer_628","name":"Jazer","kind":"City","lat":31.94353,"lon":35.72777,"summary":"He (God) helps, a city of the Amorites on the east of Jordan, and assigned, with neighbouring places in Gilead, to Gad (Num. 32:1, 35; Josh. 13:25).","verses":12,"v":[32]},{"id":"bashan_159","name":"Bashan","kind":"Region","lat":32.80008,"lon":35.9373,"summary":"Light soil, first mentioned in Gen. 14:5, where it is said that Chedorlaomer and his confederates “smote the Rephaim in Ashteroth,” where Og the king of Bashan had his residence.","verses":52,"v":[33]},{"id":"edrei_358","name":"Edrei","kind":"City","lat":32.62414,"lon":36.099,"summary":"One of the chief towns of the kingdom of Bashan (Josh. 12:4, 5). Here Og was defeated by the Israelites, and the strength of the Amorites broken (Num. 21:33-35).","verses":8,"v":[33]}],"events":[],"traditions":[["icons-and-images",8,9]],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3669,3669,3669,4428,6166,6166,3427,3427,